{
    "name": "E2E SAP Emarsys - Billing Due Date Trigger",
    "description": "End-to-end harness for the SAP Emarsys Billing Due Date trigger - the event has to be provoked by hand from an Automation Center program.",
    "notes": {
        "369b8878-1555-4e99-9f4c-5b05939571e6": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 32,
            "width": 928,
            "height": 208,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Manual provoke required - Emarsys has no billing object and no API to register a webhook\n\nThe due date lives in a custom contact date field and the event is pushed by an Automation Center\n**Webhook node**, which a human configures in the Emarsys UI. This flow is therefore a repeatable\nmanual verification harness, not an unattended test.\n\n1. In Emarsys, make sure a custom contact **date** field holds the billing due date, and that at\n   least one contact has a due date of today.\n2. Start the flow, open the **Billing Due Date** node and copy the read-only **Webhook URL**.\n3. In Emarsys go to Automation > Webhook Node Presets and create a preset that POSTs to that URL.\n   Add the contact data keys `contact_id`, `email` and the due date field under the key `due_date`\n   (it must match the node's \"Due Date Key\") - the Assert checks `contactId` and `dueDate`.\n4. Build an audience-based program with a daily **Recurring** entry point, a segment selecting the\n   contacts whose due date is coming up, and that webhook node; activate it, or send the preset\n   test delivery to fire the event immediately.\n5. \"Load All Contact Fields\" is on, so the credential also needs `contact.getdata` and `field.list`.\n6. Pause the Emarsys program before you stop this flow, otherwise the program drops into fail-safe\n   mode after repeated delivery failures.\n\nThe OnStart -> Wait lane only keeps the flow busy while you click through Emarsys - do not remove it.\nAfterAll waits 600 s for the delivery."
        }
    },
